// §14 entry 14 -- a `-or` name declared `functio` -> EXS-E0602.
//
// §3.4's suffix table: `-or` is a SUPINE-stem AGENT suffix and "must
// declare" `structura`, not `functio`. "A name whose suffix disagrees with
// its declaration is EXS-E0602. This is a well-formedness condition
// relating a name to a type, not a style lint." §3.7's own derivation table
// gives the canonical pairing this fixture violates: "lector structura
// reader" -- `lector` ("one who reads", agent of `leg-`/`lect-`) declared
// as a `structura` is correct; declared as a `functio`, below, is not.
//
// Chosen over the spec's own `[OPEN]` example (`exterior`, §4.2, flagged
// unresolved in §3.4 itself because it is a comparative `-ior`, not the
// plain agentive `-or` this rule is written for) so this fixture is not
// also exercising an open question the suite cannot yet settle either way.
//
// DEFERRED: needs the lexicon/morpheme checker (§3), which is one of this
// project's eight agents' domains outside compiler/x86_64/lexer/'s current
// scope and needs the type checker (Stage 2) to know `lector` is declared
// `functio` at all. compiler/x86_64/ast/ and cst/ are both still empty;
// `exsc aedifica`, run directly against this file, exits 0 and reports
// nothing -- confirmed, not assumed.

publica functio lector() -> textus {
    redde "lectio"
}

